## 2026-03-23 stage 8 runtime validation

- Fixed a Rust full-build blocker caused by `kernel::configfs::Subsystem::new`
  materializing a non-exported lock-class static across the module boundary.
  The abstraction now takes the lock class key from the callsite.
- Fixed a Rust runtime warning in the badblocks wrapper by matching the C
  baseline's `shift != -1` guard before calling `badblocks_check()`.
- Fixed a guest-runner defect where `wait_for_path()` clobbered the lifecycle
  loop counter in busybox `sh`, causing an infinite `cycle1` loop.
- Fixed a guest I/O tool defect where delayed writeback errors were not checked
  until `fsync()` / `close()` handling was audited and added.
- Upgraded the guest harness to use `-smp 4` so queue-count update paths are
  actually exercisable.
- Calibrated `matrix-core` to the baseline runtime environment:
  - `home_node` uses the C-compatible uint wire format
